From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:13:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] B70-QSA-D04: CPU tests for D01-D03

test_qsa_topk_levers.py checks the following:
- D01: select equals the torch selector element for element on tie-heavy
  inputs (all zeros, few values, ReLU-shaped, signed zeros, quantised, +-inf,
  randn) and across visible 0 / k-1 / k / k+1 / width; widths 1..65,728; with
  adversarial native sets (ties to the highest or a random column, unsorted);
  with the 8-bit radix schedule, with row chunks, in place over the native
  buffer, and through _topk for native_det (select and legacy) and radix.
  Under capture native_det never calls the native op. The debug check
  rejects a wrong native set.
- D02: per-step selection is set-exact when the anchor fits; past the budget
  it is causal, equals the clipped anchor and has the expected count; it is
  inert at decode_query_len 1; expand covers only the causal prefix plus its
  tail. Skip-fit returns every visible block and only applies under the host
  bound.
- D03: the defaults, fp8 left alone, the legacy switch, the B70_QSA_TUNE
  precedence, and CPU keeping the GB300 configs.
